course: dictionary
lesson: 8738
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them in order, and the context tells you which meaning the writer means. Sermon is one of these words. «The sermon is a talk by the minister explaining a Bible passage and how to live it.» The words Bible and minister tell you this is a church talk.
explain: The second meaning is informal, so you hear it in everyday chat rather than in church. «Mum gave me a sermon about tidying my room.» Nobody is in church here. A sermon is a long, boring telling-off. Ask yourself: where are we, and who is speaking?
explain: In church, the sermon is one part of a service. «A service usually has songs, prayers, Bible readings, a sermon, often communion, and a blessing at the end.» It usually comes after the Bible readings. Catholics often call it a homily.
explain: Some sermons are famous. «Christians call it the Sermon on the Mount.» Jesus gave this great teaching on a hillside, and it is found in Matthew chapters 5 to 7. Here sermon means a talk that teaches how to live well.
fact: A sermon is a talk given during a religious service, explaining the Bible or teaching how to live.
fact: Informally, a sermon is a long, boring telling-off or lecture about how to behave.
fact: Common phrases are «preach a sermon», «give a sermon» and «the Sermon on the Mount».
fact: «The Sermon on the Mount» is Jesus' great teaching on a hillside, found in Matthew chapters 5 to 7.
fact: Catholics often say homily for the talk given in church.
exercise: «The sermon is a talk by the minister explaining a Bible passage.» What is a sermon in this sentence? | *A talk given during a church service | A bell rung before a service | A long, boring telling-off at home | A type of church song
exercise: Ben says, «Dad gave me a sermon about tidying up, and it went on for ages.» What does sermon mean here? | *A long, boring telling-off | A prayer said together | A Bible reading | A talk given in church
exercise: «Christians call it the Sermon on the Mount.» Where did Jesus give this teaching? | In a shop | In a castle | *On a hillside | At the seaside
test: In a church service, when does the sermon usually come? | At the very end, after the blessing | *After the Bible readings | Before the prayers | Before the first song
test: «Noah kicked the pew all through the sermon (the priest's long talk).» What does sermon mean in this sentence? | A short prayer at the door | A type of seat | A song sung by the choir | *A long talk from the priest
exam: Which meaning of sermon is informal, the kind you hear in everyday talk? | *A long, boring telling-off | A prayer said together | A part of the Bible | A talk given by a priest in church
